    m_MinSize: 3
    m_MaxSize: 229
    m_Alignment: 0
    m_AlignByGeometry: 0
    m_RichText: 1
    m_HorizontalOverflow: 0
    m_VerticalOverflow: 1
    m_LineSpacing: 1
  m_Text: 'I built a hardware-software system built with Python, OpenCV, and a Raspberry
    Pi that uses real-time computer vision to analyze gameplay from an external video
    feed and automatically translate detected game states into controller inputs.
    In the examples shown, I did not touch the controller at all while the robot
    played the game for me. The system operates with ZERO software or hardware modifications
    to the game or gaming system, relying entirely on external visual input. The
    project features image detection and classification, real-time frame processing,
    automated decision logic, hardware I/O integration, and responsive input execution,
    achieving roughly a 95% success rate compared with human players.

'
